\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{What the two arms jointly establish, stated formally.}{34}{section*.41}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{prop:nonidentifiability_full}{{12}{34}{Empirical non-identifiability of preservation levels; Proposition~\ref {prop:nonidentifiability} of the body, restated with proof}{theorem.12}{}}
\newlabel{prop:rho_deltac}{{13}{34}{$\rho $ and $\Delta _c$ are independently controllable}{theorem.13}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{The dissociation is not Krum-specific: all four aggregators, all four channels.}{35}{section*.42}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{A second dataset and a differently configured CNN, pre-registered.}{35}{section*.44}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A8}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The four channels, all four aggregators, under Mode~S.} Endpoint change $\kappa {=}0 \to \kappa {=}2$. \textbf  {The last three channels are the levels of Def.~\ref {def:levels}}, decision $P_3$, admission $P_4$ and ASR $P_5$, so every row is a filled-in $\Delta P_3$--$\Delta P_5$ report of the kind §\ref {sec:protocol}'s clause~(4) asks for, and the arm is classified by the highest level preservation survives at; $P_1$ and $P_2$ need no measurement, being settled algebraically by Prop.~\ref {prop:invariance} before any run, and their columns are absent for that reason rather than unrun. \textbf  {The first column, $\Delta $~agg., is the relative displacement of the aggregate the defense \emph  {emits}}, $\|\mathrm  {agg}(T(U)) - \mathrm  {agg}(U)\|/\|\mathrm  {agg}(U)\|$: what enters training, and \textbf  {not} the value of a scoring statistic; the measured channels are aggregate displacement, decision, admission and influence. The dissociation between the \emph  {decision} channel and the \emph  {admission} channel is not a property of one aggregator: it holds for a selector, a cosine-invariant selector, a coordinate-wise order statistic and a weighted averager. \textbf  {The two channels do not have equal room, and the $\Delta $~adm.\ column is a support flip rather than a magnitude}: averaged over the rounds an adversary joins, the pre-transform admitted fraction is $0.000$ on every Krum row and $0.083$ on Cosine-Krum, which is one round in twelve, against $0.286$ on coord.\ median and $0.0014$ on reputation, each nonzero in all twelve. So the decision reading rests on Krum, whose decision channel is unconstrained and moves on $0.733$ of rounds, and the admission reading rests on coord.\ median and reputation, the two arms with room; a zero on a Krum row is a floor and is not evidence either way. The table does \textbf  {not} order the arms ($\Delta \Lambda _a$ and $\Delta $ASR disagree in rank, which is this section's refutation stated in one row-pair) and it is \emph  {not} an out-of-sample test: all rows are Mode-S ladders reported elsewhere in this paper. \textbf  {The sixth row is the score-only control}: the same arm as the first with the magnitude channel closed, so its $\Delta $~agg.\ is the re-selection component alone and its decision, admission and influence columns are the first row's own numbers, score-only leaving the selection untouched. \textbf  {That is why its $0.986$ \emph  {exceeds} the first row's $0.892$ with the magnitude channel closed}: $0.892$ is the vector sum of that same $0.986$ re-selection component and a $0.973$ rescaling component, which partly cancel, so a larger number in this column is a \emph  {narrower} channel and not a wider one (§\ref {app:decomposition}). \textbf  {The seventh row varies architecture alone}: the first row's cell on \texttt  {resnet18} instead of \texttt  {cifar\_cnn}, with dataset, $N$, $K$, $f$, $\alpha $, attack and defense all at their frozen CIFAR-10 values, so it is the only row that differs from the first in a single factor. Its channel columns were measured \emph  {prospectively} (\texttt  {results/\allowbreak  resnet18\_\allowbreak  admission.json} records ``No ASR. Freezes nothing.'' and predates every ResNet18 ASR in this paper), and its two unrun interior rungs are why §\ref {app:resnet18_dose} reports no trend statistic for it. \textbf  {$n$ is the seed count behind the $\Delta $~ASR column and nothing else}: the channel columns are per-round measurements, whose counts are given above. It is emitted per row as \texttt  {n\_seeds} $= \min (n_0,n_2)$ over the row's two rungs and it is \textbf  {not uniform}, reading $3$ for the second-dataset replication, $8$ for \texttt  {cos\_krum} and $20$ for the score-only row. \textbf  {That last pair of cells is the one thing in this table the emitter does not produce, and we say so rather than let the two disagree silently}: \texttt  {build\_channel\_table.py} reads \texttt  {results/\allowbreak  score\_only/} and returns the published $n{=}5$ contrast, $-0.023$, whereas what is printed here is the $n{=}20$ top-up of App.~\ref {app:score_only_n20}, assembled from three artifacts by that arm's own analyzer with both legs' seed sets asserted first. So row~6's $\Delta $~ASR and $n$ are read from an analyzer rather than from the emitter, and \emph  {both} values stand at their own seed counts, $-0.023$ at $n{=}5$ in App.~\ref {app:score_only} and $-0.009$ at $n{=}20$ here. The emitter also records \texttt  {seeds\_match} on the six rows whose two rungs come from one paired suite, and it is true on all six; the score-only row's ASR is read from a separate directory, so it carries no such field.}}{36}{table.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:channels_full}{{A8}{36}{\textbf {The four channels, all four aggregators, under Mode~S.} Endpoint change $\kappa {=}0 \to \kappa {=}2$. \textbf {The last three channels are the levels of Def.~\ref {def:levels}}, decision $P_3$, admission $P_4$ and ASR $P_5$, so every row is a filled-in $\Delta P_3$--$\Delta P_5$ report of the kind §\ref {sec:protocol}'s clause~(4) asks for, and the arm is classified by the highest level preservation survives at; $P_1$ and $P_2$ need no measurement, being settled algebraically by Prop.~\ref {prop:invariance} before any run, and their columns are absent for that reason rather than unrun. \textbf {The first column, $\Delta $~agg., is the relative displacement of the aggregate the defense \emph {emits}}, $\|\mathrm {agg}(T(U)) - \mathrm {agg}(U)\|/\|\mathrm {agg}(U)\|$: what enters training, and \textbf {not} the value of a scoring statistic; the measured channels are aggregate displacement, decision, admission and influence. The dissociation between the \emph {decision} channel and the \emph {admission} channel is not a property of one aggregator: it holds for a selector, a cosine-invariant selector, a coordinate-wise order statistic and a weighted averager. \textbf {The two channels do not have equal room, and the $\Delta $~adm.\ column is a support flip rather than a magnitude}: averaged over the rounds an adversary joins, the pre-transform admitted fraction is $0.000$ on every Krum row and $0.083$ on Cosine-Krum, which is one round in twelve, against $0.286$ on coord.\ median and $0.0014$ on reputation, each nonzero in all twelve. So the decision reading rests on Krum, whose decision channel is unconstrained and moves on $0.733$ of rounds, and the admission reading rests on coord.\ median and reputation, the two arms with room; a zero on a Krum row is a floor and is not evidence either way. The table does \textbf {not} order the arms ($\Delta \Lambda _a$ and $\Delta $ASR disagree in rank, which is this section's refutation stated in one row-pair) and it is \emph {not} an out-of-sample test: all rows are Mode-S ladders reported elsewhere in this paper. \textbf {The sixth row is the score-only control}: the same arm as the first with the magnitude channel closed, so its $\Delta $~agg.\ is the re-selection component alone and its decision, admission and influence columns are the first row's own numbers, score-only leaving the selection untouched. \textbf {That is why its $0.986$ \emph {exceeds} the first row's $0.892$ with the magnitude channel closed}: $0.892$ is the vector sum of that same $0.986$ re-selection component and a $0.973$ rescaling component, which partly cancel, so a larger number in this column is a \emph {narrower} channel and not a wider one (§\ref {app:decomposition}). \textbf {The seventh row varies architecture alone}: the first row's cell on \texttt {resnet18} instead of \texttt {cifar\_cnn}, with dataset, $N$, $K$, $f$, $\alpha $, attack and defense all at their frozen CIFAR-10 values, so it is the only row that differs from the first in a single factor. Its channel columns were measured \emph {prospectively} (\texttt {results/\allowbreak resnet18\_\allowbreak admission.json} records ``No ASR. Freezes nothing.'' and predates every ResNet18 ASR in this paper), and its two unrun interior rungs are why §\ref {app:resnet18_dose} reports no trend statistic for it. \textbf {$n$ is the seed count behind the $\Delta $~ASR column and nothing else}: the channel columns are per-round measurements, whose counts are given above. It is emitted per row as \texttt {n\_seeds} $= \min (n_0,n_2)$ over the row's two rungs and it is \textbf {not uniform}, reading $3$ for the second-dataset replication, $8$ for \texttt {cos\_krum} and $20$ for the score-only row. \textbf {That last pair of cells is the one thing in this table the emitter does not produce, and we say so rather than let the two disagree silently}: \texttt {build\_channel\_table.py} reads \texttt {results/\allowbreak score\_only/} and returns the published $n{=}5$ contrast, $-0.023$, whereas what is printed here is the $n{=}20$ top-up of App.~\ref {app:score_only_n20}, assembled from three artifacts by that arm's own analyzer with both legs' seed sets asserted first. So row~6's $\Delta $~ASR and $n$ are read from an analyzer rather than from the emitter, and \emph {both} values stand at their own seed counts, $-0.023$ at $n{=}5$ in App.~\ref {app:score_only} and $-0.009$ at $n{=}20$ here. The emitter also records \texttt {seeds\_match} on the six rows whose two rungs come from one paired suite, and it is true on all six; the score-only row's ASR is read from a separate directory, so it carries no such field}{table.caption.43}{}}
