\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A19}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The evidence ledger in one object.} One row per claim class: the tier of evidence behind it, the seed count where a seed count applies, and its status. Nothing in this table is new; every row is stated with its provenance in this section's provenance paragraph, in Table~\ref {tab:tiers}, or in Table~\ref {tab:channels_full}. \textbf  {The $n$ column is not uniform and its rows are never pooled}: a row is supported at its own $n$ and tier and at no other, which is why the adjudicating arm and its three replications are listed separately rather than as one finding at $n{=}16$. A dash means the claim is algebraic, or that no single seed count stands behind it.}}{80}{table.caption.62}\protected@file@percent }
